From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:16:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] builds on machines of your own: Linux and Windows
 runners, Linux choices

Self-hosted runners cost no Actions minutes. The workflow side
(pullify, patches 0008/0009) lets every job of the Linux, Windows and
macOS workflows and of their helper workflows go to the runner label in
a repository variable (RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX, RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX_ARM,
RDGEN_RUNNER_WINDOWS; the Mac jobs have their own), skips the cleanup
that frees disk on GitHub's images when on a self-hosted runner, and
checks a self-hosted Linux or Windows runner's prerequisites first.

Inside an LXC, ARM builds and AppImage/Flatpak are not expected to
work, so the form gets two Linux choices, sent to the workflow only
when they are not the default: "Linux builds" (x86_64 and ARM, x86_64
only, ARM only -> input linux_arch) and "Linux packages" (everything,
or .deb and .rpm only -> input linux_formats). The JSON API takes
linuxArch and linuxFormats.

SETUP-PULL.md: the runner variables, what a Linux and a Windows runner
need, and the costs per platform.

