+### Builds on machines of your own (self-hosted runners)
+
+Jobs on a self-hosted runner cost no Actions minutes. Every job of the Linux, Windows and macOS workflows, and of the helper workflows they call (setup, bridge, cleanup, the Windows top-most-window helper), picks its machine from a repository variable (**Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables**) and falls back to GitHub's when it is not set:
+
+| Variable | Jobs | Set it to |
+|---|---|---|
+| `RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX` | Linux x86_64 builds and all helper jobs | the label of a Linux x86_64 runner, e.g. `rdgen-linux` |
+| `RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX_ARM` | Linux aarch64 builds | an ARM Linux runner (rarely needed) |
+| `RDGEN_RUNNER_WINDOWS` | Windows builds | the label of a Windows runner, e.g. `rdgen-windows` |
+| `RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_X86_64`, `RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_AARCH64` | Mac builds | the label of an Intel or an Apple Silicon Mac runner |
+
+With all of the ones you build for set, a build uses no GitHub-hosted minutes at all, so it keeps working under a $0 budget. Android always runs on GitHub (its jobs need the Android SDK of GitHub's image).
+
+On a self-hosted runner the workflows skip the cleanup that frees disk on GitHub's throwaway images (`sudo rm -rf /opt/ghc ...`), and the Linux and Windows build jobs first check their prerequisites and say what is missing.
+
+**Linux:** an Ubuntu 22.04 machine with Docker (the build runs in containers; `/dev/fuse` must exist) and passwordless `sudo` for the runner user, used for nothing else: the build action prunes all Docker images before and after each build. In the RustDesk LXC setup, `tools/runner-lxc.sh` creates such an LXC on the Proxmox host. An x86_64 machine cannot run the ARM jobs (they need ARM hardware, or QEMU registered on the host), so choose **Linux builds: x86_64 only**, or set `RDGEN_RUNNER_LINUX_ARM` to an ARM runner. **Linux packages: .deb and .rpm only** is the safest choice in an LXC. The swap step of the build only runs on GitHub's machines (an LXC may not enable swap; give the container enough RAM and swap instead). RustDesk 1.5.0's extra DRM build (an unattended Wayland .deb) runs on a Linux runner of yours only when the repository variable `RDGEN_LINUX_DRM` is `true`: it takes that runner for most of an hour.
+
+**Windows:** Windows with Visual Studio 2022 Build Tools (C++), Git for Windows (`bash`), PowerShell 7, Python 3, Chocolatey, NuGet and the .NET SDK, and the runner service running as an administrator. In the RustDesk LXC setup, `tools/runner-windows.ps1` installs all of it on a Windows Server VM.
+
 ### Mac builds on a Mac of your own
 
 Jobs on a self-hosted runner cost no Actions minutes. The Mac jobs can run on your own Mac:
@@ -72,7 +91,7 @@ Jobs on a self-hosted runner cost no Actions minutes. The Mac jobs can run on yo
 3. In the build repository: **Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables**: set `RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_X86_64` (Intel Mac) or `RDGEN_RUNNER_MACOS_AARCH64` (Apple Silicon Mac) to that label.
 4. On the form, set **Mac builds** to the kind of Mac the runner is.
 
